{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare","title":"cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.md","line":163,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex#cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-segment-inequality]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex","label":"cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare","line":321,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[weak Poincaré inequality]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0301,petersen:page-0302}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch7-segment-inequality}\n  \\dcref{ch7:7.1.11}\n  Assume $(M,g)$ has $\\Ric\\ge(n-1)k$, $k\\le0$. Any smooth $u:M\\to[0,\\infty)$\n  satisfies\n  \\[\n    \\|u-u_{B(p,R)}\\|_{1,B(p,R)}\\le4C^2R\\,\\|du\\|_{1,B(p,2R)},\n  \\]\n  where $R\\le D$ and $C=C(n,kD^2)$ is as in \\cref{thm:pet-ch7-segment-inequality}.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare,thm:pet-ch7-segment-inequality,lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison}\n  \\sketch\n  For \\(B=B(p,R)\\), integrate \\(|u(x)-u(y)|\\) along chosen minimizing segments in \\(B(p,2R)\\). The segment inequality bounds the triple integral of \\(|du|\\), and \\cref{lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison} bounds \\(\\vol B(p,2R)/\\vol B(p,R)\\), giving the stated \\(4C^2R\\) estimate.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[weak Poincaré inequality] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a7065742d6368372d7765616b2d706f696e63617265\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0301, petersen:page-0302</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-segment-inequality\">↗ thm:pet-ch7-segment-inequality</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:7.1.11</span></span>Assume <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> has <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ric \\ge (n-1)k$\">$\\Ric \\ge (n-1)k$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k\\le 0$\">$k\\le 0$</span>. Any smooth <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u:M\\to [0,\\infty )$\">$u:M\\to [0,\\infty )$</span> satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\| u-u_{B(p,R)}\\| _{1,B(p,R)}\\le 4C^2R\\, \\| du\\| _{1,B(p,2R)},  \\]\">\\[  \\| u-u_{B(p,R)}\\| _{1,B(p,R)}\\le 4C^2R\\, \\| du\\| _{1,B(p,2R)},  \\]</span> where <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$R\\le D$\">$R\\le D$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$C=C(n,kD^2)$\">$C=C(n,kD^2)$</span> is as in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-segment-inequality\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-segment-inequality\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368372d7365676d656e742d696e657175616c697479\">subsection 1.5</a>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23cor%3Apet-ch7-weak-poincare\">↗ cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-segment-inequality\">↗ thm:pet-ch7-segment-inequality</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23lem%3Apet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison\">↗ lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison</a> \\sketch For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B=B(p,R)$\">$B=B(p,R)$</span>, integrate <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|u(x)-u(y)|$\">$|u(x)-u(y)|$</span> along chosen minimizing segments in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B(p,2R)$\">$B(p,2R)$</span>. The segment inequality bounds the triple integral of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|du|$\">$|du|$</span>, and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23lem%3Apet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368372d72656c61746976652d766f6c756d652d636f6d70617269736f6e\">subsection 1.2</a> bounds <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\vol B(p,2R)/\\vol B(p,R)$\">$\\vol B(p,2R)/\\vol B(p,R)$</span>, giving the stated <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$4C^2R$\">$4C^2R$</span> estimate. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-segment-inequality","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapte